      ],
      "source": "https://harvardhistory.org/navigation-history/"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "Harvard’s historic common is framed by colonial and Victorian homes, churches, town hall, and library, preserving a rural town feel.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        11
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 2"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.harvard-ma.gov/379/History-of-Harvard"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "The town’s early economy included a lucrative ice trade, with clear ponds producing hard, compact ice for regional markets.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
